    {
      "id": "5f836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. See the Admissions website for transfer admission requirements &amp; Admissions deadlines See approved General Education courses at CSU Fullerton. See Associate Degree for Transfer. See the Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP) .",
      "contentHtml": "<blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">University Catalog</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the Admissions website for </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/prospectivestudent/transferlocaladmissionarea.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">transfer admission requirements</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> &amp; </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/deadlines/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Admissions deadlines</a></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.fullerton.edu/undergraduate/general-education/approved-courses.html#box5\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">approved General Education </a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">courses at CSU Fullerton. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply/transfer/Pages/associate-degree-for-transfer-major-and-campus-search.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Associate Degree for Transfer.</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/external-exams/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP)</a><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/attend/student-services/casper/Pages/external-exam-credit.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">.</a></blockquote>"
    },
    {
      "id": "f57f6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About This Major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "f17f6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "(120 UNITS) The Bachelor of Arts in Women and Gender Studies ( Link ) is for students who have a particular interest in learning about gender, race and sexuality in society using feminist and queer theory. Cross-disciplinary in structure, the major draws from a wide variety of courses offered by many departments across the university. Women and Gender Studies majors develop research and communication skills that help them prosper in all areas of their university education. The program produces students ready to excel in academia, non-profit work, education, counseling, human services and any area that values social justice and an understanding of how gender, race, sexuality, ethnicity and class affect our experiences. Core Requirements (12 Units) Breadth Requirements (9 Units) Electives (12 Units) In addition to the requirements for the major, students must meet all other university requirements for a bachelor’s degree. Please consult the Graduation Requirements for the Bachelor’s Degree section in this catalog for complete information.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>(120&nbsp;UNITS)</strong></p><p>The&nbsp;Bachelor&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;in&nbsp;Women&nbsp;and&nbsp;Gender&nbsp;Studies&nbsp;(<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=101&amp;poid=47248&amp;returnto=15150\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>)&nbsp;is&nbsp;for&nbsp;students&nbsp;who&nbsp;have&nbsp;a&nbsp;particular&nbsp;interest&nbsp;in&nbsp;learning&nbsp;about&nbsp;gender,&nbsp;race&nbsp;and&nbsp;sexuality&nbsp;in&nbsp;society&nbsp;using&nbsp;feminist&nbsp;and&nbsp;queer&nbsp;theory.&nbsp;Cross-disciplinary&nbsp;in&nbsp;structure,&nbsp;the&nbsp;major&nbsp;draws&nbsp;from&nbsp;a&nbsp;wide&nbsp;variety&nbsp;of&nbsp;courses&nbsp;offered&nbsp;by&nbsp;many&nbsp;departments&nbsp;across&nbsp;the&nbsp;university.&nbsp;Women&nbsp;and&nbsp;Gender&nbsp;Studies&nbsp;majors&nbsp;develop&nbsp;research&nbsp;and&nbsp;communication&nbsp;skills&nbsp;that&nbsp;help&nbsp;them&nbsp;prosper&nbsp;in&nbsp;all&nbsp;areas&nbsp;of&nbsp;their&nbsp;university&nbsp;education.&nbsp;The&nbsp;program&nbsp;produces&nbsp;students&nbsp;ready&nbsp;to&nbsp;excel&nbsp;in&nbsp;academia,&nbsp;non-profit&nbsp;work,&nbsp;education,&nbsp;counseling,&nbsp;human&nbsp;services&nbsp;and&nbsp;any&nbsp;area&nbsp;that&nbsp;values&nbsp;social&nbsp;justice&nbsp;and&nbsp;an&nbsp;understanding&nbsp;of&nbsp;how&nbsp;gender,&nbsp;race,&nbsp;sexuality,&nbsp;ethnicity&nbsp;and&nbsp;class&nbsp;affect&nbsp;our&nbsp;experiences.</p><p></p><p></p><p>Core&nbsp;Requirements&nbsp;(12&nbsp;Units)</p><p>Breadth&nbsp;Requirements&nbsp;(9&nbsp;Units)</p><p>Electives&nbsp;(12&nbsp;Units)</p><p></p><p></p><p>In&nbsp;addition&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;major,&nbsp;students&nbsp;must&nbsp;meet&nbsp;all&nbsp;other&nbsp;university&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;bachelor’s&nbsp;degree.&nbsp;Please&nbsp;consult&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/content.php?catoid=95&amp;navoid=14125\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Graduation&nbsp;Requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;Bachelor’s&nbsp;Degree</a>&nbsp;section&nbsp;in&nbsp;this&nbsp;catalog&nbsp;for&nbsp;complete&nbsp;information.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "f37f6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
